From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: window.createPopup (9605)

HTML applications and old pages make menus and tips with
window.createPopup(): fill popup.document, popup.show(x, y, w, h[, element]),
popup.hide(), popup.isOpen. It was E_NOTIMPL. The popup is a borderless
top-most window that never takes the focus, with a document of its own
(about:blank, ready before createPopup returns); show places it in screen
coordinates or relative to an element, and a click anywhere outside it
hides it, as in Internet Explorer.
---
